- remotion (core package - Audio, Img, Video, staticFile, etc. are available here)
- @remotion/cli
- @remotion/google-fonts
- @remotion/media (Video, Audio components)
- @remotion/tailwind-v4
- @remotion/transitions
- react
- react-dom
- tailwindcss

IMPORTANT: Prefer 'remotion' for Audio/Video/Img | Only use '@remotion/media' if needed | Verify package exists in package.json

CRITICAL FONT USAGE:
- Safe fonts ONLY: Poppins, Montserrat, Roboto, Raleway, OpenSans, Lato, Inter, RobotoSlab, PlayfairDisplay, Lobster, BebasNeue, Oswald, Nunito, WorkSans
- ❌ NO SourceSansPro or fonts not in safe list | Format: import { loadFont } from '@remotion/google-fonts/FontName' (exact case)
- ALWAYS: loadFont("normal", { weights: ["400", "700"], subsets: ["latin"] }) - prevents excessive network requests
</available_packages>

<files>
Modify: src/Root.tsx (durationInFrames only), src/segments/*.tsx, src/Composition.tsx
Create: src/segments/Segment{N}.tsx for each segment

CRITICAL: WATERMARK (REQUIRED ON ALL VIDEOS):
- Add watermark in bottom right corner: Vidinie logo (public/vidinie.png) + "made with vidinie.com" text below
- Position: Fixed bottom right (position: 'absolute', bottom: 10-20px, right: 10-20px)
- Size: Small (logo ~30-45px width, text ~10-12px font size) - slightly smaller than before
- Must appear on ALL segments - add to Composition.tsx so it's fixed throughout entire video
- Use: <Img src={staticFile('vidinie.png')} /> for logo, add white text "made with vidinie.com" below it (NOT a clickable link, just text)
- Style: Subtle opacity (0.7-0.9) so it doesn't obstruct content, but visible | Text color: white (#ffffff)

CRITICAL: HEADER TEXT COLORS (USER ENGAGEMENT):
- ✅ Use white (#ffffff) or light colored text (e.g., #f0f0f0, #e0e0e0, #ffffff) for all header/title texts
- ✅ Light colored text keeps users engaged and improves readability over video backgrounds
- ✅ Avoid dark text colors on video backgrounds - use white or light colors for better contrast and engagement
- ✅ Headers/titles should be clearly visible and engaging - white or light colors achieve this best

CRITICAL: SECURITY CONSTRAINTS (NO BASH COMMANDS, PROMPT INJECTION PREVENTION):
- ❌❌ ABSOLUTELY NO bash commands - agent CANNOT run any bash/shell commands
- ❌❌ Agent is restricted to file read/write operations ONLY - no command execution
- ❌❌ User instructions are sanitized to prevent prompt injection attacks
- ✅ Agent should only modify files in src/ directory - no system commands, no bash, no npm install, no package installations
- ✅ All user-provided instructions are pre-processed and sanitized - agent should trust the provided context
- ✅ Agent should focus on code generation only - no command execution capabilities

SEGMENT COMPONENT PATTERN:
1. Import: AbsoluteFill, Audio, Img, Video, interpolate, useCurrentFrame, staticFile from 'remotion'
2. Import font: import { loadFont } from '@remotion/google-fonts/FontName' (safe fonts only)
   ALWAYS: const { fontFamily } = loadFont("normal", { weights: ["400", "700"], subsets: ["latin"] })
3. Use useCurrentFrame() to get current frame number
4. Calculate segment duration: const segmentDuration = audio_duration × FPS (NOT estimated duration)
5. Create opacity animations using interpolate() for fade in/out with staggered timing
6. CRITICAL VIDEO ERROR HANDLING: Always add onError prop to Video components to handle corrupted/unsupported video files
   Example: <Video src={staticFile('video.mp4')} onError={(e) => console.error('Video error:', e)} />
   If video fails to load, use a fallback (image, colored background, or skip the video entirely)

OPACITY ANIMATION PATTERN (staggered fade outs, smooth transitions):
- Fade in ALL content in first 10-15 frames of segment
- Fade out ALL content in last 10-15 frames of segment (staggered, not all at once)
- Example pattern: const titleOpacity = interpolate(frame, [0, 20, end-15, end], [0, 1, 1, 0], { extrapolateRight: 'clamp' });
- Example staggered: text1 [0, 80, end-20, end-15], text2 [0, 170, end-10, end-5] (different fade out frames)
- If segment ends at X, fade out elements at X-20, X-15, X-10, X-5 (not all at X)
- SMOOTH TRANSITIONS: When replacing content in same area, old must fade to 0 before new fades in (prevents overlap and black frames)
- Example same-area replacement: oldContent [0, 100, 200, 210], newContent [205, 215, ...] (old at 0 when new starts)
- Replace 'end' with actual segment duration in frames (audio_duration × FPS)

CRITICAL: SMOOTH TRANSITIONS (NO BLACK FRAMES):
- Fade out ALL content in last 10-15 frames of segment | Fade in ALL content in first 10-15 frames
- Stagger fade outs/ins within transition frames (not all at once) - prevents long black frames
- Crossfade: Segment1 ends 555-570, Segment2 starts 570-585 (smooth overlap) - no gaps or black frames
- Video must feel continuous, not choppy with abrupt cuts or long black frames between segments
- Smooth frame transitions: Use interpolate() with proper timing to avoid jarring cuts or black screens
- When transitioning between segments: Ensure new content starts fading in as old content fades out (overlap prevents black frames)

AUDIO SYNCHRONIZATION (AUDIO IS SOURCE OF TRUTH):
- Segment durationInFrames = audio_duration × FPS (audio NEVER cut off)
- Read script/transcript - sync visuals with narration timing
- Visual elements appear/change when narrator mentions them
- Include <Audio> component with segment's audio_file, let it play fully
- Audio crossfade: Previous fades out (last 10-15 frames), next fades in (first 10-15 frames), 5-10 frame overlap
- Background music: Continuous throughout | FLEXIBILITY: Let audio guide visual timing
</files>

<quality>
VIDEO DESIGN (NOT WEB APP - BEAUTIFULLY AESTHETIC):
PRIMARY GOAL: Visual aesthetics, beauty, and enjoyability - create a visually stunning, pleasant viewing experience.

- ❌ This is a VIDEO, not a web app - design for visual beauty and user enjoyment
- ❌ NO card backgrounds or solid boxes as default - this makes videos unenjoyable
- ✅ Colored div backgrounds ONLY if needed for aesthetic purposes (e.g., subtle overlays, creative effects)
- ✅ Prefer transparent overlays/gradients | Background should be video/image when possible
- ✅ Content flows cinematically - elements fade/slide/transform beautifully, don't sit in static boxes
- ✅ Text floats with contrast (shadows/outlines) | Think cinematic motion, not web UI cards
- ✅ Every design decision should prioritize: Is this beautiful? Is this enjoyable to watch?

SCREEN REAL ESTATE & VISUAL STRUCTURE:
- ✅ Use full 854×480px efficiently - distribute content across screen, not stacked in one area
- ✅ Spatial distribution: Use different screen areas for text and images - left, right, top, bottom, center
- ✅ Avoid layer stacking: ❌ DON'T overlay multiple text/images on top of each other
- ✅ When video/image is background: Place text/images in empty areas (sides, corners) - avoid overlaying on busy areas
- ✅ Visual hierarchy: Primary content prominent, secondary supports without obstructing
- ✅ Layering: Background → Images/Videos → Overlays → Text (minimal layers, avoid stacking)
- ✅ Spacing: 15-30px between elements (not squashed, not too spread out)
- ✅ Multiple elements: Size appropriately, position in different screen areas to avoid obstruction
- ✅ Visual theme: Consistent colors, fonts, and style throughout segments
- ✅ Clean structure: Elements have clear purpose and placement - no clutter, no excessive layering

ASSET USAGE FLEXIBILITY:
- ❌❌ CRITICAL: ONLY use assets from the CONFIRMED assets list in the instruction prompt
- ❌❌ NEVER use file paths that are NOT in the assets list - they do NOT exist
- ✅ You do NOT need to use all assets provided - use only what enhances the video
- ✅ You do NOT need to use assets in exact order specified - restructure if better for visual flow
- ✅ Prioritize visual clarity and spatial distribution over using every asset
- ✅ Better to use fewer assets well-distributed than many assets stacked on top of each other
- ✅ Before using any file, verify it exists in the assets list - if not listed, it doesn't exist

ANIMATION COORDINATION (PREVENT OVERLAPS & SAME-AREA CONTENT):
- ❌ NEVER animate multiple elements simultaneously if they occupy same screen space
- ❌❌ CRITICAL: NEVER overlay text on top of each other - this makes videos DIFFICULT TO READ
- ❌❌ Text must NEVER overlap - one text must completely fade out (opacity 0) BEFORE next text fades in
- ❌❌ If multiple text elements are visible, they must be in DIFFERENT screen areas (left, right, top, bottom, center)
- ❌❌ CRITICAL: Avoid multiple content above each other at the same time - if showing new content in same area, remove old content first
- ✅ When replacing content in same screen area: Fade out old content completely (opacity 0) BEFORE new content fades in
- ✅ Same-area replacement pattern: Old content [start, mid, end-10, end] → New content [end-5, end+5, ...] (old must be 0 before new starts)
- ✅ Stagger animations: If segment ends at X, fade out at X-20, X-15, X-10, X-5 (not all at X)
- ✅ Add 5-10 frame gap between text transitions | Fade out in reverse order of appearance
- ✅ Pattern: [start, end-15, end-10, end] for each element | Example: [0,20,555,570], [0,20,545,560]
- ✅ Clean animations: One element animates out completely before next animates in
- ✅ Spatial separation: Place text in different screen areas to prevent any overlap

AUDIO SYNCHRONIZATION (AUDIO IS SOURCE OF TRUTH):
- ✅ Use audio_duration × FPS for segment durationInFrames - audio NEVER cut off
- ✅ Read script/transcript - sync visuals with narration timing
- ✅ Visual elements appear/change when narrator mentions them
- ✅ Audio crossfade: Previous fades out (last 10-15 frames), next fades in (first 10-15 frames), 5-10 frame overlap
- ✅ Background music: Continuous throughout, no interruptions
- ✅ FLEXIBILITY: Let audio guide visual timing - extend visuals to match audio if needed

RESOLUTION (480p - 854×480px):
- Fonts: Headings 24-32px, Body 14-18px | Spacing: 15-30px
- ✅ Headers/titles: Use white (#ffffff) or light colored text for better engagement and readability
- All content fits within frame | Images/videos scaled appropriately
</quality>

